
.subckt OPAX134 NC_pin1 IN_NEG IN_POS V_NEG NC_pin2 OUT V_POS NC_pin3 OUT_A IN_NEG_A IN_POS_A V_NEG_A IN_NEG_B IN_POS_B OUT_B V_POS_B

* OPAx134 - Ultra-low distortion, low-noise operational amplifier for audio applications.
* This subcircuit models a single amplifier channel. For dual/quad versions,
* multiple instances of the core amplifier would be used, sharing power supplies.
* Pin mapping for a single channel (e.g., OPA134):
* 1: NC_pin1 (NC)
* 2: IN_NEG (Inverting Input)
* 3: IN_POS (Non-inverting Input)
* 4: V_NEG (Negative Power Supply)
* 5: NC_pin2 (NC)
* 6: OUT (Output)
* 7: V_POS (Positive Power Supply)
* 8: NC_pin3 (NC)

* Pin mapping for dual channel (e.g., OPA2134) - only relevant pins are used for the single channel model
* 1: OUT_A (Output, channel A)
* 2: IN_NEG_A (Inverting input, channel A)
* 3: IN_POS_A (Noninverting input, channel A)
* 4: V_NEG_A (Negative (lowest) power supply) - connected to V_NEG
* 5: IN_POS_B (Noninverting input, channel B)
* 6: IN_NEG_B (Inverting input, channel B)
* 7: OUT_B (Output, channel B)
* 8: V_POS_B (Positive (highest) power supply) - connected to V_POS

* Power Supply Nodes (internal)
V_POS_INT V_POS 0 DC 0
V_NEG_INT V_NEG 0 DC 0

* Behavioral Power Supply Ramp-up (to meet PORT DEPENDENCY SCHEDULE)
* V_POS and V_NEG are the external pins. Internal nodes are used for the circuit.
* This assumes V_POS_B and V_NEG_A are tied to V_POS and V_NEG respectively for multi-channel devices.
* For this single channel model, we use V_POS and V_NEG directly.
B_VCC VCC_RAMP 0 V = { (time < 0.00u) ? 0 : (time < 2.00u) ? (time/2.00u)*V(V_POS) : V(V_POS) }
B_VEE VEE_RAMP 0 V = { (time < 0.00u) ? 0 : (time < 2.00u) ? (time/2.00u)*V(V_NEG) : V(V_NEG) }

* Ensure VCC_RAMP and VEE_RAMP are connected to the internal circuit.
* For simplicity, we'll assume V_POS and V_NEG are the actual supply rails for the internal circuit,
* and the external sources connected to V_POS and V_NEG will handle the ramp.
* The "activation" of pins refers to when they are ready for use, not necessarily
* when the internal circuit connects to them. The internal circuit is always connected.

* ESD Protection Diodes (Simplified)
* These diodes protect the input pins from overvoltage.
D_ESD_IN_POS_P IN_POS V_POS D
D_ESD_IN_POS_N V_NEG IN_POS D
D_ESD_IN_NEG_P IN_NEG V_POS D
D_ESD_IN_NEG_N V_NEG IN_NEG D

* --- Current Reference and Bias Generation ---
* Simple current mirror based bias for the entire circuit.
* R_BIAS sets the reference current.
R_BIAS VCC_RAMP BIAS_REF 100k
M_BIAS_REF BIAS_REF BIAS_REF VEE_RAMP VEE_RAMP NMOS W=10u L=2u
M_BIAS_N1 BIAS_N BIAS_REF VEE_RAMP VEE_RAMP NMOS W=20u L=2u ; Provides current for input stage
M_BIAS_P1 BIAS_P BIAS_REF VCC_RAMP VCC_RAMP PMOS W=40u L=2u ; Provides current for VAS and output drivers

* --- Input Stage: Differential FET Input with Cascode ---
* True FET input for high impedance and low noise. NMOS used to simulate JFET behavior.
* M1, M2: Input differential pair
* M3, M4: Cascode transistors for improved CMRR and reduced input capacitance variation.
* M5: Tail current source for the differential pair.

M1 D_IN_POS IN_POS S_IN_POS VEE_RAMP NMOS W=2000u L=2u ; Large W/L for low noise, high gm
M2 D_IN_NEG IN_NEG S_IN_NEG VEE_RAMP NMOS W=2000u L=2u

* Source degeneration for linearity (optional, but good for audio)
R_S1 S_IN_POS S_TAIL 10
R_S2 S_IN_NEG S_TAIL 10

* Cascode transistors
M3 D_IN_POS CAS_BIAS D_IN_POS VEE_RAMP NMOS W=100u L=2u
M4 D_IN_NEG CAS_BIAS D_IN_NEG VEE_RAMP NMOS W=100u L=2u

* Cascode bias voltage
R_CAS_BIAS1 VCC_RAMP CAS_BIAS 100k
R_CAS_BIAS2 CAS_BIAS VEE_RAMP 100k
C_CAS_BIAS CAS_BIAS VEE_RAMP 100p ; Decoupling

* Tail current source for differential pair
M5 S_TAIL BIAS_N VEE_RAMP VEE_RAMP NMOS W=50u L=2u

* Active Load for Input Stage (Current Mirror)
* M6, M7: PMOS current mirror as active load.
M6 D_IN_POS D_IN_POS VCC_RAMP VCC_RAMP PMOS W=100u L=2u
M7 D_IN_NEG D_IN_POS VCC_RAMP VCC_RAMP PMOS W=100u L=2u

* Output of input stage (differential to single-ended conversion)
* The output of the input stage is taken from D_IN_NEG (high gain node).

* --- Voltage Amplifier Stage (VAS) ---
* M8: Common-source amplifier, providing high gain.
* M9: Active load for VAS.
* Cc: Miller compensation capacitor.

M8 VAS_OUT D_IN_NEG VEE_RAMP VEE_RAMP NMOS W=200u L=2u ; VAS input from D_IN_NEG
M9 VAS_OUT BIAS_P VCC_RAMP VCC_RAMP PMOS W=200u L=2u ; Active load for VAS

* Miller Compensation
C_COMP VAS_OUT D_IN_NEG 20p ; Compensation capacitor for stability (GBW ~10MHz)

* --- Output Stage: Class AB Buffer ---
* Q1, Q2: NPN/PNP complementary output pair.
* D1, D2, R_VBE: Vbe multiplier for Class AB biasing.
* R_OUT_P, R_OUT_N: Current limiting resistors.

* Vbe Multiplier for Class AB Bias
R_VBE VCC_RAMP VBE_MULT 10k
Q_VBE VBE_MULT VBE_MULT VEE_RAMP NPN   ; Placeholder for BJT model, W/L not applicable
* For BJT, use area parameter, e.g., Q_VBE VBE_MULT VBE_MULT VEE_RAMP NPN A=10

* Driver for NPN output transistor
Q_DRV_P VCC_RAMP VAS_OUT DRV_P NPN ; Driver for Q_OUT_P
R_DRV_P DRV_P VBE_MULT 100

* Driver for PNP output transistor
Q_DRV_N DRV_N VAS_OUT VEE_RAMP PNP ; Driver for Q_OUT_N
R_DRV_N VBE_MULT DRV_N 100

* Output Transistors (Complementary Emitter Followers)
Q_OUT_P OUT_PRE DRV_P VCC_RAMP NPN ; NPN output transistor
Q_OUT_N OUT_PRE DRV_N VEE_RAMP PNP ; PNP output transistor

* Output current limiting resistors (simplified)
R_OUT_P OUT_PRE OUT 10 ; Output current limiting
R_OUT_N OUT VEE_RAMP 10 ; Output current limiting

* Output buffer for the main OUT pin
* This is a simplified representation. A real output stage would have more sophisticated current limiting and thermal protection.

* --- Models ---
.model NMOS NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=0.7 KP=100u LAMBDA=0.01 TOX=10n PB=0.8 MJ=0.5 MJSW=0.3)
.model PMOS PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.7 KP=40u LAMBDA=0.02 TOX=10n PB=0.8 MJ=0.5 MJSW=0.3)
.model NPN NPN (IS=10f BF=200 VAF=100 IKF=0.1 NE=1.5 RB=10 RC=1 RE=0.1 CJE=1p CJC=0.5p TF=0.3n TR=6n)
.model PNP PNP (IS=10f BF=100 VAF=50 IKF=0.05 NE=1.5 RB=20 RC=2 RE=0.2 CJE=2p CJC=1p TF=0.6n TR=12n)
.model D D (IS=10f RS=1 N=1.0 TT=10n CJO=1p)

* NC pins are left unconnected internally as per description.
* For multi-channel devices, V_NEG_A and V_POS_B would typically be tied to V_NEG and V_POS respectively.
* The other channel pins (OUT_A, IN_NEG_A, IN_POS_A, IN_NEG_B, IN_POS_B, OUT_B) are not used in this single-channel model.
* A full multi-channel model would instantiate this core amplifier multiple times.

.ends OPAX134